  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Georgia: Addressing Drivers of Health-Related Migration to Switzerland (Georgia Cares)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is intended as a preparatory phase of a mid to long term intervention with the overall objective of addressing drivers of health-related migration from Georgia to Western European countries such as Switzerland and Austria. Lack of trust toward the local medical system, lack of information about medical services available, limited availability or unaffordable price of specialized medical treatment in the domestic health care system have all been important drivers of irregular migration from Georgia to Europe in the past years. IOM will seek to consolidate information and analyses on the issue, in order to enhance understanding of the root causes and draw conclusions and recommendations, as well as to actively engage relevant stakeholders and establish a coordination mechanism between them to facilitate multi-sectoral and joint action planning. Based on this preparatory work, IOM hopes to inform a following, more solution-oriented intervention, in which the root causes of medically driven irregular migration are addressed through structural and individual level actions.</narrative>
  </description>
